      "title": "What major medical is",
      "narration": "Major medical insurance is the comprehensive plan most people mean by health insurance. It covers a broad range of hospital, surgical, physician, diagnostic, prescription and preventive services, with high or unlimited maximums, in exchange for cost sharing by the insured. Historically it was sold as a supplement over a basic hospital plan or as a comprehensive plan standing alone; today the comprehensive form dominates. Federal law forbids lifetime and annual dollar limits on essential health benefits and caps the insured’s annual out-of-pocket spending. Common exclusions remain: cosmetic surgery, experimental treatment, custodial care, and adult dental and vision.",
