      "title": "Work the numbers",
      "narration": "Marcus’s plan has a 3,000 dollar deductible, 80/20 coinsurance and a 6,000 dollar out-of-pocket maximum. A hospital stay produces 20,000 dollars of allowed charges. He pays the first 3,000. Of the remaining 17,000 he owes 20 percent, which is 3,400, for a total of 6,400. But his out-of-pocket maximum is 6,000, so he pays 6,000 and the insurer pays 14,000. If a second claim arrives in December, the plan pays 100 percent because he has already reached the maximum. The arithmetic is always deductible first, coinsurance second, cap last.",
