      "title": "What counts toward the out-of-pocket maximum",
      "text": "The federal annual limit counts deductibles, coinsurance and copayments for in-network essential health benefits. It does not count premiums, balance bills from out-of-network providers, or spending on services the plan does not cover. For 2026 the federal ceiling is $10,150 for self-only and $20,300 for family coverage; plans may set lower limits.",
