      "title": "Embedded versus aggregate family deductibles",
      "text": "An embedded family deductible lets one family member’s coverage begin once that person meets the individual deductible, even if the family total is not met. An aggregate deductible requires the whole family amount before anyone’s coverage begins. Federal rules require an embedded individual out-of-pocket limit within family plans.",
      "example": "Elena meets her $3,000 individual deductible in March; her claims are covered even though the $6,000 family deductible is unmet.",
